        "type": "capacitor",
        "farads": 1e-7
      },
      "blurb": "Sits within two millimeters of U1's VCC pin to act as a local charge reservoir that shunts high-frequency switching transients to ground. At steady state DC it behaves as an open circuit and draws zero current."
